# Sunken Citadel's two restricted mana, "Spend this mana only to activate abilities of land sources" (CR 106.6), and the
# pool emptying at the end of each step and phase (CR 106.4).
# Turn 3: with only the Citadel's {U}{U} in the pool (the Island tapped for Aether Spellbomb), Ponder can't be cast and
# neither of the Spellbomb's abilities - an artifact's, not a land's - can be activated. The {U}{U} is lost when the
# main phase ends. Turn 5: one restricted {U} pays Sunken Ruins' {U/B}, an ability of a land, for {U}{U} of its own;
# that unrestricted mana casts Ponder and pays the Spellbomb's {U}. The other restricted {U} waits in the pool through
# Ponder's resolution, the same step, and is gone in the next phase.

